{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>עד</b>. This is a noble parable, and the bucket (גולה) is at the top of the turning wheel (גלגל) by a rope, and the top of the rope is tied to the bucket." "<b>וירתק</b> [is] from the making of a rope (עשה הרתוק). When the rope is bound tight, it is as though it hangs down and cannot reach the spring. Likewise the matter of the word ירחק, which is written, and the word ונרוץ is from ותרץ את גלגלתו, from the matter of וירוצצו, when the bucket breaks." "<b>וירוץ הגלגל אל הבור</b>. The jug breaks and no water rises, and the word ונרוץ is nif'al pattern like נכון, a singular past verb, from נכונו ללצים שפטים." "<b>וחבל הכסף</b>. This is the spinal cord, and he called it silver because it is white." "<b>וגולת הזהב</b>. This is the brain, and he likened it to gold because of the membrane that is red, which is upon it. And the jug (כד) is the gallbladder, and it is called כד because there the red bile joins together." "<b>והמבוע</b>. This is the liver." "<b>ונרוץ הגלגל</b>. The skull of the head, which was above, has gone down into the pit beneath the earth."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:21.541517310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}